      "dependents_count": 1,
      "first_30_lines": "\"\"\"\nembedding_service.py \u2014 OpenAI + Gemini Embedding Generation\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: What are embeddings?\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nAn embedding is a list of floating-point numbers (a vector)\nthat represents the MEANING of a piece of text.\n\nExample:\n    \"The employee cannot work for competitors\"\n    \u2192 [0.023, -0.847, 0.112, ..., 0.334]  \u2190 1536 numbers\n\nTwo sentences with similar meaning will have vectors that are\n\"close together\" in 1536-dimensional space.\n\n\"The employee cannot work for competitors\"\n\"Non-compete clause applies for 2 years\"\n\u2192 These vectors will be CLOSE (similar meaning)\n\n\"The employee cannot work for competitors\"  \n\"The cat sat on the mat\"\n\u2192 These vectors will be FAR APART (different meaning)\n\nThis is how semantic search works:\n1. Store all chunk embeddings in Pinecone\n2. When user asks a question, embed the question too\n3. Find the 5 chunks whose embeddings are closest to the question embedding\n4. Those 5 chunks are the most relevant context\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Why a service module for embeddings?",
