      "first_30_lines": "\"\"\"\nuser.py \u2014 User Data Models\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Pydantic v2 Models\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPydantic models are Python classes that:\n1. Define the SHAPE of your data (like TypeScript interfaces)\n2. VALIDATE data automatically (raise errors if wrong type)\n3. SERIALIZE/DESERIALIZE data (dict \u2194 model object)\n\nThink of them as Zod schemas + TypeScript interfaces combined.\n\nTypeScript equivalent:\n    interface UserCreate {\n        email: string;\n        password: string;\n        name: string;\n    }\n\nPydantic equivalent:\n    class UserCreate(BaseModel):\n        email: EmailStr\n        password: str\n        name: str\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Multiple Models for Same Entity\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWe use separate models for different stages:\n  UserCreate   \u2192 What the client SENDS (includes password)\n  UserInDB     \u2192 What's STORED in MongoDB (hashed password)",
