      "first_30_lines": "\"\"\"\ndocument.py \u2014 Document Data Models\n\nThis file defines the shape of data for uploaded PDF documents.\nIt covers three stages:\n  1. What gets stored in MongoDB (DocumentInDB)\n  2. What the API returns to the client (DocumentResponse)\n  3. The chunk structure stored alongside documents (ChunkMetadata)\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Enum\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nAn Enum (enumeration) is a set of named constants.\nInstead of using raw strings like \"processing\", \"ready\", \"failed\"\neverywhere (which can have typos), we define them once in an Enum.\n\nThis is exactly like TypeScript's:\n    type DocumentStatus = \"processing\" | \"ready\" | \"failed\"\n\nBut stronger \u2014 Python will raise an error if you try to set\na status that's not in the enum.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom enum import Enum\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Status Enum \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n",
