      "dependents_count": 6,
      "first_30_lines": "\"\"\"\nconfig.py \u2014 Central Configuration\n\nPYTHON CONCEPT: Pydantic Settings\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n`BaseSettings` is like a Pydantic model but designed\nspecifically for environment variables. It:\n  1. Reads from your .env file automatically\n  2. Validates the types (str, int, bool)\n  3. Raises a clear error at startup if something is missing\n\nThink of it like dotenv + Zod combined in one class.\n\nWhen you write:\n    settings = Settings()\nPython reads every variable from .env and maps them\nto the class fields by name. If OPENAI_API_KEY is missing\nfrom .env, you get an error immediately \u2014 not later when\nyou try to use it.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom pydantic_settings import BaseSettings, SettingsConfigDict\nfrom pydantic import Field\nfrom functools import lru_cache   # Python built-in caching decorator\nfrom typing import Literal         # For constraining string values to a set\n\n\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Singleton Pattern with lru_cache \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500",
